<title>FRANCE: EP wants Singapore to review farm trade.</title>
<headline>EP wants Singapore to review farm trade.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament said on Thursday the European Union should use the December meeting of the World Trade Organisation to study the impact of farm sector reform on countries that are net importers of foodstuffs.</p>
<p>It also called for a thorough review of import arrangements for farm products, export subsidies and domestic aid.</p>
<p>In several sectors, the standards of the WTO Codex Alimentarius were not appropriate for the EU and the Union should therefore reserve the right to impose tougher norms, the parliament said in a resolution.</p>
<p>They said the EU should use the ministerial conference, which takes place next month in Singapore, to insist the WTO take more account of environmental problems.</p>
</text>
